  "configuration_id": "config_006",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_005 (rna_only, multiprofile, scvi_n200, avgpool) achieved 0.650 acc / 0.628 F1, a dramatic ~13-point gain over its singleprofile counterpart (config_004, 0.520). This makes multiprofile + scvi_n200 the clearly dominant direction. However, we have only tested one aggregation strategy (avgpool) for this setting. The aggregation method is the critical mechanism that determines how multiple profiles are combined, and transformer-based aggregation could capture inter-profile relationships that simple averaging discards. Question: Does transformer aggregation outperform avgpool for multiprofile scvi_n200, and if so, by how much? Why this is the best next experiment: It is the most direct exploitation of our strongest result while resolving a high-uncertainty design choice (aggregation) that could meaningfully shift performance. A large gap would justify further transformer-based multimodal experiments; a small gap would confirm avgpool sufficiency and redirect budget toward other levers (e.g., adding image in multiprofile mode). Under a limited budget, clarifying this binary choice before branching into multimodal multiprofile variants is the most information-efficient use of the next run."
}

